  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Who checks",
      "items": [
        "run_bench_net.sh: gate_verdict() judges the snapshots in gates_<host>.txt (five values first against last; active throttling, the highest temperature and other busy processes in any snapshot) and the footers and headers of the CSV files, and writes EXCLUDED with the reason; NOTE_* files are recorded, not judged.",
        "Harness run: the driver puts the output of check_csv.py and check_clock_probe.py --form into check.txt. Gateway run (run_e2e.sh, marker FUNCTIONAL): the driver puts the output of check_run.py into check.txt; that driver writes no gates_<host>.txt and no EXCLUDED.",
        "make_tables.py marks every number of a DRY_RUN, PILOT or EXCLUDED run as not a result; merge_numbers.py stops on such an input unless --allow-marked.",
        "A reader in campaign/own/ recomputes the quantities from the raw files with its own code and compares them key by key with numbers.csv.",
        "The driver writes MANIFEST.sha256 last, with shasum -a 256 over the files of runs/<run_id>/; no program in the repository reads or verifies it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Documented, not enforced by this code",
      "items": [
        "Acceptance of a run (driver status 0, no EXCLUDED file, the second reader agrees) is a documented procedure. accepted_runs.tsv records its outcome: run directory, key prefix and reader, or - where no reader was compared. No program in the repository reads the list.",
        "merge_numbers.py merges the analysis directories it is given; it reads no list and no reader verdict.",
        "The article reads the merged file with \\input and prints each number as \\meas{key}; an unknown key is a LaTeX error unless the article defines \\measundefined before the \\input."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not in this repository",
      "items": [
        "The run directories: runs/ is ignored by git. The drivers create them on the driver machine; they are archived with the dataset, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24506181 (docs/CAMPAIGN.md calls accepted_runs.tsv the run index of the dataset).",
        "The scripts that sequenced the measurement sessions; the README says they are archived with the dataset.",
        "The analysis outputs, numbers_all.tex and the article.",
        "Not drawn: single-board runs (run_single_node.sh on a board), which accepted_runs.tsv lists as well."
      ]
    }
  ]
